  'course.basics.title': 'The basics',
  'course.basics.intro': 'Sketch, extrude, then add <dfn data-term="feature">features</dfn> on top. Every part in Fusion is made this way.',
  'course.robot.title': 'Design your robot arm',
  'course.robot.intro': 'Design the parts of a small robot arm, then assemble them with joints and make it move. Print the parts and join them with M3 screws.',
  'course.elf.title': 'Elf furniture',
  'course.elf.intro': 'Make furniture for a dollhouse. Elves are tiny: everything here is 12 times smaller than real furniture.',
  'lesson.robot-base.title': 'Robot base',
  'lesson.robot-base.intro': 'Every robot arm starts with a strong base: a round plate with two tabs on top. The first arm link turns on a screw between the tabs.',
  'lesson.robot-base.steps': [
    'Click <b>Create Sketch</b> and pick the <b>XY</b> plane. Draw a <b>Circle</b> with Center <b>0</b>, <b>0</b> and Diameter <b>60</b>.',
    'Click <b>Finish Sketch</b>, then <b>Extrude</b> it <b>6</b> mm.',
    'Create a sketch on the <b>top face</b>. Draw two <b>Rectangles</b>, Width <b>4</b> and Height <b>20</b>: one at Center <b>-6</b>, <b>0</b>, one at Center <b>6</b>, <b>0</b>. Click <b>Finish Sketch</b>.',
    '<b>Extrude</b> the two tabs <b>24</b> mm up.',
    'Click <b>Hole</b>, then the <b>outside face</b> of a tab. On a side face, Y is the height. Set X <b>0</b>, Y <b>24</b>, Diameter <b>3.5</b>, Depth <b>0</b>. The hole goes through both tabs!',
  ],
  'lesson.robot-base.outro': 'The hole is 3.5 mm, a little bigger than the 3 mm screw, so the arm can turn. Engineers call that gap <dfn data-term="clearance">clearance</dfn>.',
  'lesson.robot-link.title': 'Arm link',
  'lesson.robot-link.intro': 'An arm link is a bar with round ends and a hole at each end. Shapes that overlap in a sketch join together, so a rectangle and two circles make the round ends.',
  'lesson.robot-link.steps': [
    'Create a sketch on the <b>XY</b> plane. Draw a <b>Rectangle</b>: Center <b>0</b>, <b>0</b>, Width <b>48</b>, Height <b>12</b>.',
    'Add two <b>Circles</b> of Diameter <b>12</b>, at Center <b>-24</b>, <b>0</b> and <b>24</b>, <b>0</b>. Click <b>Finish Sketch</b>.',
    '<b>Extrude</b> it <b>6</b> mm.',
    'Add two <b>Holes</b> on the top face, Diameter <b>3.5</b>, all the way through: one at X <b>-24</b>, one at X <b>24</b> (Y <b>0</b>).',
  ],
  'lesson.robot-link.outro': 'The holes are 48 mm apart. Print two links and your arm can bend twice. Want a longer arm? Try the challenge.',
  'lesson.robot-finger.title': 'Gripper finger',
  'lesson.robot-finger.intro': 'Not every part is a rectangle or a circle. The <b>Line</b> tool draws any shape, one corner at a time. The numbers next to the cursor tell you where you are.',
  'lesson.robot-finger.steps': [
    'Create a sketch on the <b>XY</b> plane and pick <b>Line</b>. Click these corners in order: <b>-20, -14</b> → <b>-14, -14</b> → <b>-14, 0</b> → <b>20, 0</b> → <b>20, 6</b> → <b>-20, 6</b>. Then click the first one again to close the shape.',
    'Click <b>Finish Sketch</b> and <b>Extrude</b> it <b>5</b> mm.',
    'Add a <b>Hole</b> on the top face for the pivot screw: X <b>14</b>, Y <b>3</b>, Diameter <b>3.5</b>, Depth <b>0</b>.',
    'Inside corners are where parts break. Add a <b>Fillet</b> with Radius <b>2</b> on the inside corner of the hook.',
  ],
  'lesson.robot-finger.outro': 'Print two fingers, mirror one in your <dfn data-term="slicer">slicer</dfn>, and you have a gripper. In Fusion, the Line tool works the same way, and you can type each length.',
  'challenge.robot-longlink.title': 'Long arm link',
  'challenge.robot-longlink.brief': [
    'A bar 12 wide and 6 thick, with round ends, centered on the origin',
    'The round ends are centered at X -40 and X 40',
    'Holes Ø3.5 all the way through at both ends',
  ],
  'lesson.elf-table.title': 'Elf table',
  'lesson.elf-table.intro': 'Let’s furnish an elf house! A table is 4 legs and a top. You can draw all 4 legs in one sketch.',
  'lesson.elf-table.steps': [
    'Create a sketch on the <b>XY</b> plane. Draw 4 <b>Circles</b> of Diameter <b>6</b>, at Center <b>-35, -20</b>, <b>35, -20</b>, <b>35, 20</b> and <b>-35, 20</b>.',
    'Click <b>Finish Sketch</b> and <b>Extrude</b> the legs <b>40</b> mm.',
    'Create a sketch on the <b>top of a leg</b>. The sketch covers the whole flat plane, not just the leg. Draw a <b>Rectangle</b>: Center <b>0</b>, <b>0</b>, Width <b>80</b>, Height <b>50</b>. Click <b>Finish Sketch</b>.',
    '<b>Extrude</b> the table top <b>4</b> mm with <b>Join</b>.',
    'Round the corners of the table top: <b>Fillet</b> its 4 standing edges with Radius <b>5</b>.',
  ],
  'lesson.elf-table.outro': 'To 3D print it, turn it upside down in your <dfn data-term="slicer">slicer</dfn>. The top lies flat on the bed and the legs point up, so no supports are needed.',
  'lesson.elf-chair.title': 'Elf chair',
  'lesson.elf-chair.intro': 'A chair is a small table with a back. This time the legs are square.',
  'lesson.elf-chair.steps': [
    'On the <b>XY</b> plane, draw 4 <b>Rectangles</b> of <b>4</b> × <b>4</b> at Center <b>-13, -13</b>, <b>13, -13</b>, <b>13, 13</b> and <b>-13, 13</b>. Finish the sketch and <b>Extrude</b> the legs <b>25</b> mm.',
    'Sketch on the <b>top of a leg</b> and draw the seat: Center <b>0</b>, <b>0</b>, Width <b>30</b>, Height <b>30</b>. Finish and <b>Extrude</b> it <b>3</b> mm.',
    'Sketch on the <b>top of the seat</b> and draw the back: Center <b>0</b>, <b>13.5</b>, Width <b>30</b>, Height <b>3</b>. Finish and <b>Extrude</b> it <b>30</b> mm.',
    'Round the top of the back: <b>Fillet</b> its 2 short top edges with Radius <b>5</b>.',
  ],
  'lesson.elf-chair.outro': 'Drawing 4 legs one by one is slow. In Fusion, a <dfn data-term="pattern">Rectangular Pattern</dfn> copies one leg for you. Look for it when you get there!',
  'lesson.elf-shelf.title': 'Elf bookshelf',
  'lesson.elf-shelf.intro': 'You can sketch on the side of a part too. Here you cut 3 shelf spaces into the front of a tall box.',
  'lesson.elf-shelf.steps': [
    'On the <b>XY</b> plane, draw a <b>Rectangle</b>: Center <b>0</b>, <b>0</b>, Width <b>50</b>, Height <b>20</b>. Finish and <b>Extrude</b> it <b>70</b> mm.',
    'Create a sketch on the <b>wide front face</b>. On a side face, Y is the height. Draw 3 <b>Rectangles</b> of Width <b>44</b> and Height <b>18</b>, at Center <b>0, 13</b>, <b>0, 35</b> and <b>0, 57</b>. Click <b>Finish Sketch</b>.',
    '<b>Extrude</b> with Distance <b>-16</b> and Operation <b>Cut</b>.',
  ],
  'lesson.elf-shelf.outro': 'The shelves are what is left between the cuts. Start with a block, then take away what you don’t need: real designers do that all the time.',
  'challenge.elf-bed.title': 'Elf bed',
  'challenge.elf-bed.brief': [
    'Bed base 40 × 70, 8 tall, centered on the origin',
    'Headboard on top of the base, at the back end: 40 wide, 4 thick (Y from 31 to 35), 25 tall',
    'Pillow on top of the base: 24 × 10 (Y from 17 to 27), 4 tall, with its 4 standing edges rounded: radius 3',
  ],

  'group.assemble': 'ASSEMBLE',
  'tool.joint': 'Joint',
  'tool.drive': 'Drive Joints',
  'feature.joint': 'Joint',
